# Cenários de análise NF-e × EFD ICMS/IPI, com as regras M1 do NUCLEO-2 (dados sintéticos).
# Cliente: extensão REST Client (humao.rest-client). Clique em "Send Request" acima de cada bloco.
# Os lotes ficam em exemplos/cenarios/ e cada um tem o mesmo resultado verificado em CenariosNfeEfdTests.
#
# Antes de usar:
#   1. docker compose -f docker-compose.rag.yml up -d
#   2. ./scripts/preparar-http.ps1             (grava os tokens locais no .env, que não é versionado)
#   3. Suba as duas APIs: F5 com "Api.RAG + Api.Agente"
#
# Atenção: com Parecer:Habilitado = true nos user-secrets, cada análise chama a OpenAI e gera custo.
#
# O que olhar na resposta:
#   resultado.status          situação da análise
#   resultado.achados         regra, severidade, valores dos dois lados, diferença e hipóteses legítimas
#   resultado.regras          situação de cada uma das 10 regras
#   resultado.fundamentacao   trechos do RAG por regra com achado
#   parecer                   texto do LLM, sempre sujeito a revisão humana

@agente = http://localhost:5117
@rag = http://localhost:5203
@tokenAgente = {{$dotenv AGENTE_TOKEN}}


###############################################################################
# 1. Saúde dos serviços
###############################################################################

### 1.1 Api.Agente
GET {{agente}}/health

### 1.2 Api.RAG
GET {{rag}}/health


###############################################################################
# 2. Controle positivo
###############################################################################

### 2.1 Tudo coerente → CONCLUIDA, sem achados, sem revisão humana
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-01-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/01-consistente.json


###############################################################################
# 3. Inconsistências de presença e lastro (M1.1 e M1.2)
###############################################################################

### 3.1 NF-e de venda sem C100 → M1-P01 grave; M1-I01 não conclusiva; CONCLUIDA_PARCIAL
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-02-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/02-omissao-saida.json

### 3.2 NF-e cancelada escriturada como regular → M1-P02 alerta e M1-R01 grave
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-05-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/05-cancelada-escriturada-regular.json

### 3.3 C100 cancelado sem evento na NF-e → M1-R02 e M1-P01 graves (indício de débito omitido)
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-06-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/06-cancelado-sem-evento.json

### 3.4 Documentos de outro estabelecimento → M1-R03 e M1-R04 graves; EFD da filial ausente em M1-P01
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-07-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/07-documento-de-outro-estabelecimento.json


###############################################################################
# 4. Inconsistências de valor e identificação (de-para M1.3)
###############################################################################

### 4.1 Valores do C100 × XML → M1-I03 (900 × 1000) e M1-I05 (BC 500 × 1000; ICMS 90 × 180)
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-03-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/03-valores-divergentes.json

### 4.2 Crédito de entrada acima do destacado → M1-I06 (250 × 60)
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-04-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/04-credito-acima-do-destacado.json

### 4.3 Número e data divergentes → M1-I01 grave (NUM_DOC) e alerta (DT_DOC)
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-08-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/08-identificacao-divergente.json


###############################################################################
# 5. Falta de evidência: nunca vira erro nem conformidade (P4, P5)
###############################################################################

### 5.1 C100 sem XML fornecido → M1-R01 ausência de evidências; CONCLUIDA_PARCIAL
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-09-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/09-c100-sem-xml.json

### 5.2 NF-e reprovada na origem → PRE-003, 9 regras sem evidências e M1-I01 não conclusiva; INCONCLUSIVA
POST {{agente}}/api/v1/analises
Authorization: Bearer {{tokenAgente}}
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-Id: cenario-10-{{$timestamp}}

< ./exemplos/cenarios/10-nfe-reprovada-na-origem.json
